# A conversation is kept on the thought tree once it is over: one node under the outcome of the
# act that opened it, read back under the pointer — what the protagonist said, how it ended and
# the chips it came to.
#
# The conversation's own screen lists those chips before its END button and is gone on the press;
# with no scrolling text behind the map there was then nowhere to read them again. This script
# wins a conversation, leaves it, and reads all of it back off the tree.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Reach the conversation through the verb that opens it.
strategy succeed
goal meet_stranger
advance 12 180
click observe "brewer"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "brewer"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
wait mode Dialogue 60
advance 20 180

# Two replies to the resolution, the roll, the outcome.
click option 0
advance 20 180
click option 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 20 180
expect Courteous, and you know when to stop

# END: back on the map, with nothing standing over it — the conversation's screen showed its chips.
click button
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
expect-not SUCCESS
expect-not CONTINUE

# The node: under the act's outcome, with both replies and everything the conversation changed.
expect-state trees act state=done verb=meet_stranger
expect-state trees dialogue with=brewer ending=success replies=2 chips=5
expect-state texts dialogue reply "My name is Kenryc Greygate."
expect-state texts dialogue reply "Good to meet you. I will not keep you from your work."
expect-state texts dialogue chip "Modus mentis learned: Hospitality"

# Under the pointer: named by whom it was with and how it ended, and read in the box at the foot
# of the map. It is a record — pointing reads it, and it is not on the clickable ground.
point dialogue last
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=grey text=talked with Aeemilyus · success
expect CONVERSATION WITH AEEMILYUS
expect "My name is Kenryc Greygate."
expect it came to: success
expect Stranger
expect Modus mentis learned: Deference
expect Modus mentis practised: Friendship

# `brewer` names the same conversation as `last`: by archetype, by role or by name.
point dialogue brewer
quit
